\begin_layout Standard
A window opened showing a waveform,
 labelled:
 HA01,
 Cape Leeuwin,
 T04:12:07Z.
 A classic ice collapse waveform:
 a descending sweep,
 eleven hertz down to four across three hundred and forty seconds.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
I knew the shape,
 the sound of ice cracking.
 I looked at the y-axis and typed.
\end_layout

