Current HA01 waveform
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Oscar displayed a new signal,
 constant and maxed out.
 The HA01 signal was the waveform of a damaged hydrophone.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\family typewriter
\series bold
Examine Crozet hydrophones,
 HA04
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Crozet is a French rock,
 significantly west of Leeuwin with three hydrophones.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Oscar repainted the window.
 Crozet had it.
 The same waveform as HA01,
 appropriately late and not maxed out,
 just unimaginable.
 We knew the detector locations and we knew ΔT.
 I turned to Oscar.
 
\end_layout

